            <ArticleTitle>Obliteration of a left main coronary artery aneurysm with a PTFE-coated stent.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>280-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The successful percutaneous obliteration of a left main coronary artery aneurysm using a covered stent (JOMED) is described. The immediate angiographic result was excellent and the early post-procedural period was uneventful. Six-month follow-up angiography revealed no changes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
